  },
  "7508588891503910912": {
   "created": 1790187094,
   "author": "Rachel Bergman",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/rachelbergman_conferences-can-be-hard-to-walk-into-alone-activity-7508588891503910912-FvwD",
   "text": "Conferences can be hard to walk into alone. I've done it too many times to count, and I've definitely been the person in the corner acting like what's going on on their phone is so important that they can't possibly talk to anyone \ud83d\ude0a.\n\nI was fortunate to be surrounded by awesomeness last week. The content, the people, the conversations (the weather!). I attended 3 events hosted by Primary Venture Partners (thank you!), all different but with common themes (ahem, AI). Each event was perfectly curated to stand alone and build on the others. \n\n4 Cool things I learned:\n\n1. I have a new favorite Harvard dropout, Gavin Uberti, the CEO of Etched. Not only is he young enough to be my kid, but he also",
   "disc_score": 15,
