  "7508650153885650944": {
   "created": 1790201700,
   "author": "Alex Pisanov",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alexpisanov_virtually-all-makers-of-cloud-ai-chips-are-activity-7508650153885650944-0wxr",
   "text": "Virtually all makers of cloud AI chips are using off-die memory \ud83d\udd75\ufe0f\u200d\u2642\ufe0f Most of them make inference ASICs.\n\nThis explains why in 2026 computer memory prices went up +100% and more in some cases \ud83d\udcc8 Let's dig a little deeper.\n\nAt a higher level, chip architectures differ in how they approach compute cores and memory (the latter also influences memory bandwidth). Two major paradigms:\n\n\ud83d\udcbbCores: general-purpose (can run both AI training and inference, and even non-AI workflows) vs. application-specific (aka ASICs; typically can run either training or inference, and are incapable of running non-AI tasks). Regardless, almost all are electronic rather than photonic (an emerging technology - developed, f",
   "disc_score": 0,
